      "my_answer": "Differentials include septic shock from other sources, streptococcal toxic shock-like syndrome (TSLS), drug reaction with eosinophilia and systemic symptoms (DRESS), viral exanthems, and Rocky Mountain spotted fever. TSS is most likely given tampon use, diffuse rash, and multiorgan involvement without alternative source.",
      "rationale": "The absence of drug exposure history makes DRESS less likely. RMSF typically has tick exposure and petechial rash. Streptococcal TSLS may present similarly but is less commonly associated with tampon use. No other infectious source is evident on exam."
